[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869012011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869012011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869012011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAaYr","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T16:49:47Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T16:53:01Z","body":"This is not a bug, it's because the underlying server is the 3D server (until 4.5), and in 4.5 it is still a `Vector3` for compatibility, we have discussed changing it however, but it is not a bug, it should probably be documented more clearly for 4.4 and earlier though regardless if we break compatibility in 4.5\n\nThis is partially documented [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/navigation/navigation_using_navigationservers.html#d-and-3d-navigationserver-differences)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869012011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869021529","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869021529","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869021529,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rActZ","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T16:53:10Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T16:53:10Z","body":"For Godot 4.5 with the split to the dedicated NavigationServer2D we should imo use that event to break compatibility and change it from Vector3 to Vector2.\n\nFor Godot 4.3 or 4.4 it is too late to change that. What we could do is update / extend the agent script example found [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/navigation/navigation_using_navigationagents.html#navigationagent-script-templates) (above the agent scripts) to make it more clear that a Vector3 callback parameter is expected in those versions.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869021529/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869030620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869030620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869030620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAe7c","user":{"login":"Dan-The-Assassin","id":54580180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTgwMTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54580180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin","html_url":"https://github.com/Dan-The-Assassin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T17:05:17Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T17:05:17Z","body":"> This is not a bug, it's because the underlying server is the 3D server (until 4.5), and in 4.5 it is still a `Vector3` for compatibility, we have discussed changing it however, but it is not a bug, it should probably be documented more clearly for 4.4 and earlier though regardless if we break compatibility in 4.5\n> \n> This is partially documented [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/navigation/navigation_using_navigationservers.html#d-and-3d-navigationserver-differences)\n\nIs it not a bug that the agent does not do avoidance though?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869030620/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869031335","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869031335","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869031335,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAfGn","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T17:06:35Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T17:06:35Z","body":"The vector is converted as detailed in the documentation I linked, it should be `Vector3(vel.x, 0.0, vel.y)`, not using the `y`","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869031335/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869035015","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869035015","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869035015,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAgAH","user":{"login":"Dan-The-Assassin","id":54580180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTgwMTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54580180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin","html_url":"https://github.com/Dan-The-Assassin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T17:11:50Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T17:12:07Z","body":"Using it as such, for example with a code like the following, the character bodies 2D move, yes, but there is no avoidance.\n```   private void onVelocityComputed(Vector3 safeVelocity)\n    {\n        Velocity = new Vector2(safeVelocity.X, safeVelocity.Z);\n        MoveAndSlide();\n    }","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869035015/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869035811","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869035811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869035811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAgMj","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T17:13:48Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T17:16:48Z","body":"> Is it not a bug that the agent does not do avoidance though?\n\nThis might be an issue with a node or script conflict e.g. shadowing some properties or functions on the node class, or even some C# specific issue.\n\nThis basic gdscript used on a generic Node2D works just fine (tested in Godot 4.4.1):\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\nvar agent: RID\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tagent = NavigationServer2D.agent_create()\n\tNavigationServer2D.agent_set_map(agent, get_world_2d().navigation_map)\n\tNavigationServer2D.agent_set_avoidance_enabled(agent, true)\n\tNavigationServer2D.agent_set_avoidance_callback(agent, Callable(self, \"_avoidance_done\"))\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta: float) -> void:\n\tNavigationServer2D.agent_set_position(agent, global_position)\n\tNavigationServer2D.agent_set_velocity(agent, Vector2(10.0, 15.0))\n\nfunc _avoidance_done(safe_velocity):\n\tprint(\"safe_velocity: %s\" % safe_velocity)\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869035811/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869036683","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869036683","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869036683,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAgaL","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T17:16:15Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T17:16:15Z","body":"Please provide an MRP to make this easier to test and fix:\n- A small Godot project which reproduces the issue, with no unnecessary files included. Be sure to not include the `.godot` folder in the archive (but keep `project.godot`).\n- Having an MRP is very important for contributors to be able to reproduce the bug in the same way that you are experiencing it. When testing a potential fix for the issue, contributors will use the MRP to validate that the fix is working as intended.\n- Drag and drop a ZIP archive to upload it (max 10 MB). **Do not select another field until the project is done uploading.**\n- **Note for C# users:** If your issue is *not* C#-specific, please upload a minimal reproduction project written in GDScript. This will make it easier for contributors to reproduce the issue locally as not everyone has a .NET setup available. \n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869036683/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869045038","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869045038","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869045038,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAicu","user":{"login":"Dan-The-Assassin","id":54580180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTgwMTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54580180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin","html_url":"https://github.com/Dan-The-Assassin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T17:35:35Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T17:35:35Z","body":"[testproject.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20140759/testproject.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869045038/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869045583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2869045583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2869045583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAilP","user":{"login":"Dan-The-Assassin","id":54580180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTgwMTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54580180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin","html_url":"https://github.com/Dan-The-Assassin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T17:37:13Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T17:37:13Z","body":"From my understanding, if they are given an avoidance radius and the avoidance is enabled, the safe velocity is supposed to be such as that they keep that distance from each other, but they don't. My apologies if this is a mistake on my side","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2869045583/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2891298797","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2891298797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2891298797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sVbft","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T14:42:47Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T14:44:06Z","body":"@Dan-The-Assassin I don't have a setup to test C# projects but from what I can tell looking at the script it is more or less the same as with the GDScript example so should work.\n\nIn general RVO avoidance works with velocities. Those velocities are only safe within the given time horizon under the same agent configuration. The agents, when encountering each other, pick passing sides. This means it is possible to create scenarios that break RVO avoidance. This is common with more artifical testing scenarios e.g. when agents are spawned on top of each other radius and go for perfect collision along a line it will not work because nothing finds a passing side in this case. If you really want to dig into all the details of RVO avoidance see https://www.gameaipro.com/GameAIPro3/GameAIPro3_Chapter19_RVO_and_ORCA_How_They_Really_Work.pdf ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2891298797/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2891743444","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2891743444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2891743444,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sXIDU","user":{"login":"Dan-The-Assassin","id":54580180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTgwMTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54580180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin","html_url":"https://github.com/Dan-The-Assassin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T17:15:55Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T17:15:55Z","body":"After spending another hour and trying to code this in GDScript as well, testing several agent variables and ways to give them velocity, I've found the source of my issue: unless setting the neighbor distance for the avoidance agent in code to its default value in the editor (I haven't tested other values), no avoidance will occur. This goes for both C# and GDScript. I am not sure if this behavior is intended, being given that the code you gave me as an example does not include that, the documentation doesn't mention anything like this at least.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2891743444/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2891756441","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2891756441","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2891756441,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sXLOZ","user":{"login":"Dan-The-Assassin","id":54580180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTgwMTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54580180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin","html_url":"https://github.com/Dan-The-Assassin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T17:21:18Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T17:39:04Z","body":"Here is the MRP for that. Try to comment and uncomment the neighbor distance line (line 17) and see how the avoidance behavior is present or missing based on it. (This same thing happened in the C# version as well as a bigger C# project)\n\n[testprojectgdscript.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20301434/testprojectgdscript.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2891756441/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952351033","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2952351033","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2952351033,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6v-U05","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-07T10:50:50Z","updated_at":"2025-06-07T10:52:34Z","body":"Good find. This is because in Godot 4.3 the 2D version uses the 3D version behind the scene.\n\nThe 3D version has `5.0` as its default `neighbor_distance` as it fits the 3D scale. For 2D this would translate to just 5.0 \"pixels\" so way too low and barely noticeable.\n\nWhen `NavigationAgent2D` nodes are used those nodes update all the agent properties to fit 2D better, but with a server only agent nothing updates those properties from the defaults for 2D. This is also why calling the `agent_set_neighbor_distance()` manually fixes it. Likely that issue is all the same for all those properties that would require a different scale for 2D.\n\nFor 4.3 this is a lost cause to fix as there is no real 2D server so on that version ppl need to call all those setters manually for an update.\nFor 4.5 with the dedicated NavigationServer2D this can and should be fixed. In fact that the defaults of the 2d server agent do not match the defaults on the NavigationAgent2D I would consider as mismatch bug.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952351033/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952784335","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-2952784335","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":2952784335,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6v_-nP","user":{"login":"Dan-The-Assassin","id":54580180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTgwMTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54580180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin","html_url":"https://github.com/Dan-The-Assassin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dan-The-Assassin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-07T17:27:55Z","updated_at":"2025-06-07T17:27:55Z","body":"Thank you for the response and I'm glad to hear it's going to be fine in 4.5, I think it'd also be a good idea to mention this somewhere in the documentation (the part about needing to set those values in code) in case someone else ever gets stuck with this.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952784335/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192449876","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106250#issuecomment-3192449876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106250","id":3192449876,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-SOtU","user":{"login":"stephen-polyxia","id":215675632,"node_id":"U_kgDODNry8A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/215675632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia","html_url":"https://github.com/stephen-polyxia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stephen-polyxia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-15T18:57:03Z","updated_at":"2025-08-16T11:58:16Z","body":"Is the plan to map Vector3(x, 0f, y) to Vector2(x, y) in 4.5? I spent quite a while misunderstanding and fighting with the NavigationServer2D API because of this odd mapping.\n\nEdit: removed some incorrect info from my comment","author_association":"